### P0-2: Fix Parameter Regeneration on Click

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (3-5 days)
**Dependencies**: None
**Spec Reference**: README.md line 177-183 (click-to-restart pattern) • **Status Reference**: Research decision: "Regenerate on every click"

#### Description
Currently, randomized parameters in *-varied.html and *-procedural.html files are generated once on page load. Click-to-restart uses the same parameters. User research decision: **regenerate random parameters on every click** for true variation.

**Files Affected** (40 total):
- All 20 *-varied.html files (logo + text, techniques 01-10)
- All 20 *-procedural.html files (logo + text, techniques 01-10)

**Current Pattern**:
```javascript
// Runs once on page load
const selectedMode = Random.pick(modes);
const config = { hueShift: Random.range(-15, 15), ... };

function restart() {
    startTime = null;
    // Uses same selectedMode and config
    requestAnimationFrame(animate);
}
```

**Target Pattern**:
```javascript
let selectedMode, config;

function initializeParameters() {
    selectedMode = Random.pick(modes);
    config = { hueShift: Random.range(-15, 15), ... };
    // Apply any DOM updates that depend on parameters
}

function restart() {
    initializeParameters(); // Regenerate on every restart
    startTime = null;
    requestAnimationFrame(animate);
}

// Initial setup
initializeParameters();
```

#### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] All 40 *-varied and *-procedural files updated
- [ ] Random parameters regenerate on every click/restart
- [ ] First load behavior unchanged (immediate animation start)
- [ ] Console logs show different mode/config on each click (if logging enabled)
- [ ] Visual verification: clicking shows different behavior each time
- [ ] Reduced-motion users unaffected (no animation anyway)
- [ ] No performance issues (parameter generation is lightweight)

#### Technical Notes
- **Scope per file**: Move random generation into a reusable function called by restart()
- **Watch for**:
  - DOM manipulation based on random params (e.g., setting colors in initializeParameters)
  - Timing-sensitive code that assumes params are constant
  - Animation state that needs reset (clear transforms, opacity, etc.)
- **Testing approach**:
  1. Update 1 varied + 1 procedural file (e.g., text-01-line-drawing-*)
  2. Test thoroughly: load, click 5x, verify different behavior
  3. Apply pattern to remaining 38 files
  4. Spot-check 10 random files for correctness
- **Refactoring opportunity**: Create shared utility function if pattern is identical across files

